    <string name="startup_alive_title">Keep the app alive</string>
    <string name="startup_platform_label">Detected: %1$s</string>
    <string name="platform_fyt">FYT / UIS head unit</string>
    <string name="platform_mtc">MTCD / MTCE (Microntek) head unit</string>
    <string name="platform_generic">Other Android head unit</string>
    <string name="startup_alive_fyt">Many units force-stop apps about 20 to 30 seconds after the ignition goes off, and a stopped app gets no broadcasts until you open it by hand. Add K-Line Dash to the sleep whitelist in the factory settings (Settings, then the factory menu; the code 8888 is common but differs per firmware). Newer firmware has no list there: use the FYT Factory tool instead. Open the app once after changing the list.</string>
    <string name="startup_alive_mtc">Add K-Line Dash to the list of programs that may run after sleep: \"Whitelist of programs to run after sleep\" in the Malaysk ROM, or the BootControl app on Microntek firmware. Open the app once by hand afterwards.</string>
    <string name="startup_alive_generic">Look in the settings of the unit itself for autostart, a sleep whitelist or a do-not-kill list and add K-Line Dash. Many units stop the app when the ignition goes off, and it only comes back when you open it by hand. Then allow background running with the buttons below.</string>
